You can transfer a local file to an Amazon Web Services Amazon EC2 server using the scp command.

*Syntax

scp -i <key.pem> <local-file-path> <username>@<public-ip>:<destination-path>

*Example

scp -i mykey.pem test.txt ubuntu@13.233.100.10:/home/ubuntu/


*Explanation

scp → Secure Copy command
-i mykey.pem → Private key file for EC2 access
test.txt → Local file name
ubuntu → EC2 username
13.233.100.10 → EC2 public IP address
/home/ubuntu/ → Destination path in EC2 server
Common Usernames
Ubuntu AMI → ubuntu
Amazon Linux → ec2-user
CentOS → centos


* Check the file in ec2
* Check the directory cd /home/ubuntu



